==Strategy==
The most effective way to tackle this stage is to prevent Jumbo Jones from attacking in the first place. To do this, you will want to equip the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] Battle Item for assurance.

When the stage starts, store up a shot on Sniper the Cat and disable him for now. Defeat the Metal Doge and Mr. Angels at the beginning of the stage with a combination of [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cats]], then start stacking up [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]s on the Maawth until you have a sizable amount of roughly 3-4. Once he's permanently Weakened, stack up [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]], [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom]]/[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cats]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]], and any other fast attackers you might want to use. Start sending out Jelly Dumpling Cats once it looks like Maawth is about to die. Time a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] so that he hits the base slightly after the stack of Soap Cats arrive to the enemy base, otherwise the rest of your units may not be able to catch up.

As soon as Jumbo Jones is about to spawn in, deploy the Iron Wall to stall the enemies at their base and start wailing on Jumbo Jones. If it looks like he's going to get an attack off, activate Sniper the Cat to reset his attack animation. It is recommended to use Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s to stagger the Elder Sloth more consistently, otherwise Awakened Bahamut will die the next time he attacks. The Jelly Dumpling Cats and Courier Cats should help out with this role specifically, thanks to their piercing attacks, but feel free to bring more [[Long Distance]]/[[Wave Attack|Wave]]/[[Surge Attack|Surge]] units if he proves to be an issue.

Once Jumbo Jones is dead, simply defeat the enemy base and claim victory.

